nt":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every array reserves a specific amount of memory to hold its contents.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"When you add elements to an array and that array begins to exceed its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reserved capacity, the array allocates a larger region of memory and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copies its elements into the new storage. The new storage is a multiple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the old storage’s size. This exponential growth strategy means that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"appending an element happens in constant time, averaging the performance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of many append operations. Append operations that trigger reallocation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have a performance cost, but they occur less and less often as the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grows larger."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example creates an array of integers from an array literal,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then appends the elements of another collection. Before appending, the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"array allocates new storage that is large enough store the resulting"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"elements."}]},{"code":["var numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","\/\/ numbers.count == 5","\/\/ numbers.capacity == 5","","numbers.append(contentsOf: stride(from: 60, through: 100, by: 10))","\/\/ numbers.count == 10","\/\/ numbers.capacity == 10"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Inspecting-an-Array","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Sw